{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-almost-cocontinuous}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:67bb2a7fd5b1b58ec3e31be50b044713ddec315105c52643b72e602d47228ecf", "source_text": "Almost cocontinuous functors", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cdedb08526755adfd0357e7331187748311de3814a085f1435e86d8af14d02a7", "unit_id": "tag:04B4:title"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\emptyset$", "MATH_0005": "$\\emptyset^\\#$", "MATH_0006": "$\\emptyset$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e0eb5bad92ae98c91ea9fb0ca8aaca9f68575cfd9409934e3d4a5442a73e24f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dbeb1dffb5df0000c4d75c847ea3d1f7ee4e77d4fdb892fe767f048ee7634d27", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site. The category <MATH_0002> has\nan initial object, namely the presheaf which assigns the empty set\nto each object of <MATH_0003>. Let us denote this presheaf by\n<MATH_0004>. It follows from the properties of sheafification that the\nsheafification <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> is an initial object\nof the category <MATH_0007> of sheaves on <MATH_0008>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9307b1016e868109cd25e30471d75032d4ae1803eb617d11b5e99282c3bec288", "unit_id": "tag:04B4:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\emptyset^\\# \\to h_U^\\#$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-empty}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e6a3fb815b58d174de6b76d3bd6202acc7563278d76b90ad9e331e60d7099381", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d1df6b4d24775140bf06abdb3a760be68af9e5f6852ad4888f4e6ce14bc5e68", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. We say an object <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003>\nis <TEXTITOPEN_0001>sheaf theoretically empty<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism of sheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fba7171583be7485801cbcfa676319faf154cdb255098de86e3c2603ce1f7705", "unit_id": "tag:04B5:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4c99b319ca4775a6b57e57af809dd70b66a33b7e0366c7b452b23d01893445fe", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma makes this notion more explicit.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cdbacca7cc09185ef4857df7b84c8af2fd9fc853ad141a08cb9df0c71af41023", "unit_id": "tag:04B4:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\emptyset^\\#(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\emptyset^\\#(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "MATH_0012": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0014": "$U'$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-empty}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:80c436168645abfda18a3f823a7e63d6239cadd3f9a2be4e77c678d872a78e94", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:262673e1f51243086a710c9bae88de70fce8a52b0980dbdf9541999523e3befd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is sheaf theoretically empty,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is a singleton for each sheaf <MATH_0006>,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is a singleton,\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0008> is nonempty, and\n<STRUCT_0006> the empty family is a covering of <MATH_0009> in <MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0007>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0011> is sheaf theoretically empty, then for any morphism\n<MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> the object <MATH_0014> is sheaf theoretically empty.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:215b6c918a642a4358ff4691f75f60829832325ac9afb49df00d549c8ae9eb62", "unit_id": "tag:04B6:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) = \\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U^\\#, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\emptyset^+(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\emptyset^+ = \\emptyset^\\#$", "MATH_0006": "$\\emptyset$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-plus}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-sheaf-condition-empty-covering}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-site}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fbce6c38f86dd138d4afa90bcb5b84b1e1c7c43c7acc047c2cb16ccf18f43acf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f507f412b2b7d9bde4ce40634d8fd7e272a37aac416c5f266c7f0ec651c3cac", "source_text": "For any sheaf <MATH_0001> we have\n<MATH_0002>.\nHence, we see that (1) and (2) are equivalent.\nIt is clear that (2) implies (3) implies (4).\nIf every covering of <MATH_0003> is given by a nonempty family,\nthen <MATH_0004> is empty by definition of the plus construction.\nNote that <MATH_0005> as <MATH_0006> is a separated\npresheaf, see\nTheorem <REF_0001>.\nThus we see that (4) implies (5). If (5) holds, then\n<MATH_0007> is a singleton for every sheaf <MATH_0008>\nby the sheaf condition for <MATH_0009>, see\nRemark <REF_0002>.\nThus (5) implies (2) and (1) -- (5) are equivalent. The final\nassertion of the lemma follows from Axiom (3) of\nDefinition <REF_0003>\napplied the empty covering of <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:36afae99e156d3215ad1183a1c8048222ed0bb95bd54a714dd43b6f2855032ac", "unit_id": "tag:04B6:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{V_j \\to u(U)\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$i$", "MATH_0011": "$I$", "MATH_0012": "$u(U_i)$", "MATH_0013": "$u(U_i) \\to u(U)$", "MATH_0014": "$V_j$", "MATH_0015": "$j \\in J$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-almost-cocontinuous}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1725af100c77d443bc362ae44bfb456cd1aad5af8e02289a0b564291033c31f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c38d6d38d1acc25fc32f8951ffc4c1eb925a2fbf438c463a7eb83201431a6ece", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be sites.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a functor.\nWe say <MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>almost cocontinuous<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every\nobject <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> and every covering\n<MATH_0007> there exists a covering\n<MATH_0008> in <MATH_0009> such that\nfor each <MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011> we have at least one of the following two conditions\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0012> is sheaf theoretically empty, or\n<STRUCT_0003> the morphism <MATH_0013> factors through <MATH_0014> for some <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:94c39d49e098864ca0b158860e8498a6681acdf7a5f63ee61f1a842817f42c08", "unit_id": "tag:04B7:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04B4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_{Zar} \\to Z_{Zar}$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\mapsto Z \\cap U$", "MATH_0004": "$i_*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-closed-map-cocontinuous-false}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sheaves-remark-i-star-not-exact}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:36631ffcae9addf3e48bd154137caec4f93fcae360315ebfee5bc54bb186e3f2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bd3f7809c4148c337dd14805e21dc15b2b247e9655b35c002fbc086e0a05a551", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe motivation for this definition comes from a closed immersion\n<MATH_0001> of topological spaces. As discussed in\nExample <REF_0001>\nthe continuous functor\n<MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> is\nnot cocontinuous. But it is almost cocontinuous in the sense defined above.\nWe know that <MATH_0004> while not exact on sheaves of sets, is\nexact on sheaves of abelian groups, see\nSheaves, Remark <REF_0002>.\nAnd this holds in general for continuous and almost cocontinuous functors.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2fd3324f4bb73278401db349f6b0bfc69de4f4636794a9a8c9e6d5037d56a803", "unit_id": "tag:04B4:prose-0003"}
